# Scripted events for the "play" recording (natural playing: chords, slides, glissandos), in ms on the
# recording's clock. With the settings export's switch assignments (Switch 2 and the right footswitch
# Transpose Up, the left footswitch Transpose Down), the first part transposes while chords are held,
# and returns to no transposition. The second part makes the left footswitch a sustain pedal through
# microLinn's NRPN importing, presses it twice while chords are held, and puts things back.

86000   switch 2 150         # Switch 2: Transpose Up, three or more notes held (85.2-90.25 s)
97500   pedal right down     # Transpose Up, four or more notes held (96.75-99.85 s)
97800   pedal right up
215500  pedal left down      # Transpose Down, twice: back to no transposition (three or more notes held, 214.9-223.6 s)
215800  pedal left up
216500  pedal left down
216800  pedal left up

360000  set importing 1
360100  nrpn 230 2           # Global Foot Left Assignment: Sustain
363500  pedal left down      # four or more notes held (362.75-375.4 s)
374000  pedal left up
391000  pedal left down      # three or more notes held (390.65-394.6 s), released while four are held (399.7-401.75 s)
400500  pedal left up
402000  midi B0 63 01 B0 62 66 B0 06 00 B0 26 12   # NRPN 230 = 18: the left footswitch back to Transpose Down
402100  set importing 0
